---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About HomeSpaGuide" description="Who we are, how we choose what to recommend, and how we make money — transparently.">
  <div class="container-narrow about-page">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />
    <header class="about-page__header">
      <span class="editorial-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>The trusted guide to home spas.</h1>
      <p class="lede">HomeSpaGuide is a small, independent editorial team obsessed with the home spa category. We research products, compare them in detail, and recommend what we'd actually buy ourselves.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2 id="why">Why we exist</h2>
      <p>The home spa category has hundreds of products and almost no honest buying guidance. Manufacturers' spec sheets all look the same. Amazon reviews are noisy. We exist to do the hours of research and comparison most buyers don't have time for — and then send you to the right Amazon listing.</p>

      <h2 id="how-we-choose">How we choose what to recommend</h2>
      <p>For every category we cover, we:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read every credible review and spec sheet we can find</li>
        <li>Aggregate owner feedback from Amazon, Reddit, manufacturer forums, and YouTube long-form reviews</li>
        <li>Compare published specifications side by side</li>
        <li>Filter out products with consistent complaint patterns</li>
        <li>Surface the model that best fits each buyer profile (budget, family size, climate, indoor/outdoor, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> operate a testing facility. We are an editorial curation team, not a laboratory.</p>

      <h2 id="methodology">How our Editor Score works</h2>
      <p>Our 0–10 Editor Score is a <em>curation index</em>, not a test result. It weights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Quality</strong> — build materials, manufacturer reputation, owner-reported reliability themes</li>
        <li><strong>Value</strong> — price-to-feature ratio within the category</li>
        <li><strong>Setup</strong> — reported ease of unboxing and first use</li>
        <li><strong>Durability</strong> — longevity signals from long-term owner reviews</li>
        <li><strong>Energy efficiency</strong> — published energy specs and owner-reported bill impact</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each component is a curation judgment based on the sources above — it is not a measurement. Scores can differ from Amazon's star rating because we weight criteria differently than the average reviewer.</p>

      <h2 id="badges">Editorial badges</h2>
      <p><strong>Editor Pick</strong> — the one product in a category we'd buy ourselves.</p>
      <p><strong>Best Value</strong> — best price-to-features ratio.</p>
      <p><strong>Premium Pick</strong> — the upgrade choice for buyers willing to pay more.</p>
      <p><strong>Budget Pick</strong> — the lowest price we can responsibly recommend.</p>
      <p><strong>Top Rated</strong> — consistently high satisfaction across owner reviews.</p>
      <p>Most products carry no badge. Badges are deliberately scarce.</p>

      <h2 id="affiliates">How we make money</h2>
      <p>HomeSpaGuide is an Amazon Associates participant. When you click a link and buy on Amazon, we earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. This is the only way the site sustains itself. We do not accept paid placements, sponsored reviews, or "feature my product" arrangements. Our editorial selections are not for sale.</p>

      <h2 id="prices">Why we don't show live prices</h2>
      <p>Amazon Associates rules forbid us from showing scraped or cached prices outside an approved API integration. We show a price <em>range</em> bucket instead, and the "Check price on Amazon" button always sends you to the current, accurate price.</p>

      <h2 id="team">Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>HomeSpaGuide is run by a small team of home spa owners and editors. Every article is reviewed by at least two people before publication.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions, corrections, product suggestions, or feedback? Drop us a line at <a href="/contact">our contact form</a>. We read everything.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { padding-top: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .about-page__header { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; }
  .about-page__header h1 { margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 22ch; }
  .about-page__header .lede { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: var(--text-lg); line-height: var(--leading-normal); max-width: 60ch; }
</style>
